Subject: [PATCH] feat(core): clone_get_startvoice accessor for the MCP bridge

clone_get_instance(x, n) subtracts the clone's start voice (-s) and clamps, so a walk
over instances 0..n-1 of [clone -s 1 abs N] read instance 0 twice and never the last
one. The accessor lets the caller ask for voice startvoice + i.
---
 src/g_clone.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/g_clone.c b/src/g_clone.c
index fdd06c4..ba65003 100644
--- a/src/g_clone.c
+++ b/src/g_clone.c
@@ -818,6 +818,14 @@ int clone_get_n(t_gobj *x)
     else return ((t_clone *)x)->x_n;
 }
 
+    /* plugdata MCP fork: the first voice number (-s), so a caller walking instances 0..n-1 can ask
+       clone_get_instance for voice startvoice + i (it subtracts the start voice and clamps). */
+int clone_get_startvoice(t_gobj *x)
+{
+    if (pd_class(&x->g_pd) != clone_class) return 0;
+    else return ((t_clone *)x)->x_startvoice;
+}
+
 t_glist *clone_get_instance(t_gobj *x, int n)
 {
     t_clone *c;
-- 
